      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That sense of having nowhere left to move toward is a huge weight, and it's completely understandable that the thought of simply stopping feels tempting. When the external goals fade, the internal landscape finally demands attention, and that can feel frighteningly empty. Instead of forcing a new \"mountain,\" perhaps you could explore the quiet itself, treating this stillness as a space for deep self-discovery rather than an endpoint. Even in stillness, there are ways to begin to cultivate something new within.",
